..snipped...

>bus.  We purchased a Seagate 9G drive, have tried to install it, and
>have had nothing but trouble.  We not only had difficulties in mounting
>and partitioning the drive, but it doesn't seem to want to run properly,
>i.e., it will hang the system.  Has anyone had similar problems?  Could
>the problem be with the EISA bus and/or controller card?  

In researching drives for our latest hardware I noted that Digital's branded 
9.1 GB drive (UltraSCSI) is NOT supported currently on the standard system 
SCSI controllers. Digital only supports its 9.1 GB drives on the HSZ SCSI 
controllers/hosts (to which you can connect an AlphaServer or AlphaStation).

Whether this is an operating system or a firmware issue, I don't know. But our
decision was to buy a bunch of 4.3 GB drives because we need reliability and
can't afford the administrative time in troubleshooting drive problems.

Almost certainly you'll want a later version of Digital Unix to support new 
hardware.

drew

