Ireneusz Mrozek wrote:
> 
> SYSTEM:       OSF1 v4.0 464 alpha POLYWELL
> 
> Hello,
>         I'd like to add second network adapter to my system.
> I added it physically to computer (both are PCI). I see both network
> cards in a firmwere as:
> 
>         >>> sh dev
>                         .
>                         .
>                         .
>         ewa0.0.0.6.0    EWA0    ........
>         ewb0.0.0.5.0    EWB0    ........
>                         .
>                         .
>                         .
> 
> But now network doesn't work in the UNIX (it worked before) and
> I still see only one network interface (tu0). I rebuilt kernel but
> it didn't help.
>         What can I do ?
> 
> Thanks in advance for your help
> Best regards
> 
>         Irek
> 
> --
> Ireneusz Mrozek
> 
> imrozek@pakpol.ahlstrom.com

You should reboot your machine into the generic kernel (/genvmunix)
and then build a new specific kernel when adding new hardware. This
is discussed in the management manuals - read them carefully.
If you are feeling brave, you *can* edit /sys/conf/<MACHINE_NAME> by
hand. There should be an existing line something like:

controller      tu0        at pci0      slot  6 vector    tuintr

in this file.
Adding a line like:

controller      tu1        at pci0      slot  5 vector    tuintr

and rebuilding the kernel ought to make the second card known to
the system.

I'm suspicious that the existing interface seems to have stopped
working - it suggests some clash between the two cards.
Regards,
John Hill
