Hello Ireneusz,

in order to get the new hardware recognized you have to boot
the generic kernel and then:
/usr/sbin/doconfig (including /usr/sbin/sizer)
and 
/usr/sbin/doconfig -c POLYWELL
to work in installed software and get a new kernel.

After booting the new kernel do:
/usr/sbin/netsetup
and configure the new interface with a SECOND IP address and a subnet
mask
and a otional broadcast address. Reboot.


