Andrea Toro wrote:
> 
> Many tanks for the information give to me.
> I have contacted the distributors of GEAR software and I have seen that
> this software is more expansive....the price is greater than the price
> of the cd-recorder...
> 
> I know a free-software named "Cd-record" for Linux and Solaris...do you
> know if there is a porting on Digital Unix?
> 
> Many thanks
> 
> Andrea

The free software requires a generic scsi device driver (/dev/sg) which
Digital UNIX doesn't have.  The only direct access to the scsi devices
are through the /dev/cam device that lets you send raw scsi commands to
the individual device.  You would have to translate all the /dev/sg
operations to /dev/cam operations to port cd-record.

I started on something like this about 6 months ago to work with SONY-900e
burners but got too busy to continue it.

The 'Writing Device Drivers for the SCSI/CAM Architecture Interfaces'
book documents the /dev/cam device.


Sean



