We are trying to test the VME I/F of an AXPVME 230 sbc.
In order to do this we followed the DEC documentation
available with Digital UNIX 4.0b. The documents used are:
- Writing Device Drivers: Tutorial (AA-PUBVD-TE);
- Writing VMEbus Device Drivers (AA-Q0R7F-TE), June 1997.

Following the examples provided in that documents and the
procedure to obtain either the dynamic or the static installation
and using as interrupt generator a Motorola CPU (68020 + interrupt
generator + timer PCC chip based), we observed the following behaviour:

a) with Digital UNIX it is not possible to use a simple interfacing
   mechanism different from a complete device driver; it is impossible
   to call a claim_vector mechanism or to associate an interrupt vector
   to a signal.
   Is this true?

b) The latency time observed has been 562 uS. Repeating the test
   the maximum latency time observed has been 1 mS.
   Is there a way to lower this interval time?
 
c) The memory of the AXPVME is mapped onto the VMEbus as blocks having
   8 kB size even if the user requires less. This means that the user,
   after the buffer allocation, does not have to use the unused part of
   the allocated buffer. Example: current buffer size is 1 kB,
   required data transfer 256 bytes, the DMA can transfer up to 8 kB
   and can corrupt the data from 256 to 1 kB.
   Is this true?
   
Thanks in advance.

Please e-mail to:
villani.g@laben.it



