Hallo,

Erix Molinie wrote:
> 
> Hello,
> ...
>         My problems are:
> 
>         How to use the floppy drive, I want to make a filesystem on it
>         and mount it in /floppy for example. What the name of the
>         device [ /dev/fd0a /dev/fd0c ?!? ]
>
Would You like a UNIX filesystem than do:
prompt>disklabel -wr /dev/rfd0a rx23  (RX23 is a 1.44 MB Floppy disk
	see /etc/disktab RX23 for details)
	You can verify You action with the command:
prompt>disklabel -r /dev/rfd0a
	Then make a filesystem:
prompt>newfs /dev/rfd0c rx23
	Now You have a UNIX floppy disk.
prompt>mount /dev/fd0c /mount_dir (You must create a directory for 
        the mount point)
Would You like read/write DOS floppy disks, You can use the "mtools"
include in DISGITAL UNIX operating system. Use man mtools for details.

>         Secondly there is a CD-ROM with the C++ package on it, I would
>         like to know which admin utility I need to use to install this
>         package. Does it exist an install package utility ?
>
First, You must install the license PAK for the C++ Compiler withe
the command "dxlicenses" or "lmf register".

Then mount the cdrom: mount -dr /dev/rznc /cdrom (n -s the unit number 
e.g. rz4c rz5c ...)  

Then load the cxx Compiler:
prompt> setld -l /cdrom/cxx540/kit and follow the instructions from
         the setld tool. (se also man setld)

>         Thanks in advance for your help
>         Best Regards
> 
>         Erix

Good luck and Best Regards

