> Here are more details on the kit:

In addition to the URLSs, the Adobe Acrobat Reader is built to
work with Digital UNIX 4.0B or later.  If you have an earlier
version of DIGITAL UNIX,  you will need to upgrade.


--- Installing Acrobat Reader for DIGITAL UNIX 4.0B or Later

      A beta release of the Acrobat Reader for DIGITAL UNIX is now
      available. The following sections explain how to copy, install,
      and configure the beta release. (Please note that this is a field
      test release. Adobe invites your feedback. If you encounter any
      problems, please send mail to acrobts@adobe.com specifying the
      nature of the problem and some basic system configuration
      information, including the operating system version, machine
      type/model, and video card type.)

      Copying and Installing Acrobat Reader for DIGITAL UNIX

	1.Decide which version of the Reader you wish to install, then
	  download a copy of the tar file for Acrobat Reader using
	  one of the following links:
	
ftp://ftp1.adobe.com/pub/adobe/acrobatreader/unix/3.x/acroread_osf_301.tar.Z
	
ftp://ftp1.adobe.com/pub/adobe/acrobatreader/unix/3.x/acrdsrch_osf_301.tar.Z

	2.Use the UNIX tar command to untar the files: 
		zcat my_dir/acr*.tar.Z | tar -xpvf

	3.Run the install script: 

		sh ./INSTALL 

	  Adobe installation guides are included in the tar file. 

	4.After you complete the installation, you may wish to add a
	  symbolic link to /usr/local/bin: 

	       ln -s /usr/local/Acrobat3/bin/acroread /usr/local/bin




	Hints for configuring the Acrobat Plugin for Use with Netscape
	Navigator

      The following script demonstrates how to install the Acrobat
      plugin on Digital UNIX 4.0B as root:

	  cd /usr/local/Acrobat3/Browsers/alphaosf
	  echo "nppdf.so" | cpio -pvmu /usr/lib/netscape
	  chown bin.bin /usr/lib/netscape/nppdf.so

      Then, edit the Netscape startup script, /usr/bin/X11/netscape:

	1.Search for the section titled "Copy java class libraries". 

	2.Immediately after the "fi" command, add the following lines: 

	  # 
	  # Copy the Acrobat plugin if needed 
	  # 
	  if [ ! -e $INSTDIR/nppdf.so ]; then 
	     ln -s $NLIBDIR/nppdf.so $INSTDIR/nppdf.so 
	  fi 




      Selecting Between the Plugin and Running Acrobat Reader
      Separately

      After you complete the actions in the preceding section and
      restart Netscape Navigator, Navigator will use the Acrobat plugin
      whenever you access a PDF file. If you would rather have Acrobat
      start in a separate window, complete the following steps:

	1.In Navigator, select General Preferences under the Options
	  menu. options, general preferences. 

	2.Select Helpers... from the General Preferences Dialog Box. 

	3.Select for the entry "application/pdf" and press the Edit
	  button. 

	4.Enter the following line under application: 

	       /usr/local/Acrobat/bin/acroread  %s

 
