> "How can I rebuilt my root password  If  I  forgot it  in my digital server
> 300 machine 
> with digital unix 4.0B?"
> 
> thanks...
> 
> 

Halt the machine:

* Turn on power
* Wait for "CPU 0 booting" message
* Hit Ctrl-C until you get a ">>>" prompt
* Enter 'boot -flags s'
* Wait. After a while you get a superuser prompt "#".
* Run '/sbin/bcheckrc' and '/sbin/update'
* Change root password
* Logout (the machine will continue the boot process).
* You're done

/Erik

