In article <33C1532E.27403473@orl.saic.com>, Brian Wohlschlaeger <wohlschb@orl.saic.com> writes:
>
>I need parameters that work for Fujitsu 9gig 2949Q drives.  I called
>Fujitsu and the did not have a good answer.  They had the Sun parameters
>but not the full set for BSD style disktab's.

If the disk is well behaved, Digital UNIX can get the geometry
information it wants from the drive.  It will use the default
partition table from the driver.  Once you have labeled the
drive you can repartition as you see fit.  Versions before V4.0
will use 3600 for the rotational speed, but it doesn't matter
much and you can fix it with disklabel.

Once labeled, the distributed utilities that care can get the
information they need from the label.

