This sounds like maybe you haven't registered both the BASE and DEV
licences (or CDE doesn't see the registration).  Try re-registering both
licences.

> Contact the Digital Customer Support Center @800-354-9000.  They have
> a patch available that corrects this problem.  Make sure that you
> tell them you are using the CDE ADK. (Advanced Developer's Kit which
> was the only CDE kit available for 3.2c.)

Digital's policy states that they only support two minor revs back (tech
support has repeated this to me many times)... Since the latest rev of
DUX is 4.0b, that would mean 4.0 and 4.0a are the only supported back
revs.  He's 6 minor revs out of luck with 3.2c.  Maybe the unnamed CDE
ADK rev is still supported.

Furthermore, that 800 number won't tell you the time-of-day unless you
have a support contract...(although, I think their support contract is
worth the price) even if it's a recently installed system and you've
found a bug.  Given that he doesn't have the latest rev, he doesn't get
upgrades, so I doubt he has a support contract.

Maybe you know the patch file name and it can be found at DEC's
gatekeeper archive?

Chris

