Radomir Zaric <vitez@vitez.cofc.edu> wrote in article
<33B31630.1969@vitez.cofc.edu>...
> Hi,
> 
> 	What is the size of blocks on DATs??  Should I erase them using dd
> if=/dev/zero of=tape <block size> or what else do I do??

Err, depends if you run it in fixed or variable mode, generally.
More usefully, why do you want to know .. reading back from something
that's
of unknown blocksize? / optimum settings for writes from command line
options ? /
other ? ..

Erasing them again depends on 'how' erased you'd like them. A long erase
will do everything on the media (which is what mt's erase option usually
does)
and take a _very_ long time to do it (couple of hours for DDS2), a short
erase puts
down some amble frames and then writes EOD (a few seconds time).

cheers,
al
(not speaking for HP..)



