Dave Stevens wrote:
> We wish to upgrade this machine (or rather do a new
> install) to DEC UNIX 4.0B, but both the 4.0B and 4.0A
> install CDs fail with...

My guess is your not using a DEC CD drive on this machine.  

Some non-dec drives do work, but most don't (I've tried a bunch, with
little success).  Any CD drive works for normal operation, but not for
booting from CDROM.

If I'm right, then, no ordinary CD drive will work.  I believe it has to
do with a blocking factor that is expected.  I've seen this in both
Solaris and DUX.  Once, in Solaris, we called the CD manufacturer who
new of the problem.  The solution was: for a PC, the drive will work
as-is, for a Sparc, you need to cut a trace on the drives circuit
board.  This worked.

To test this, grab the CD drive off of one of your other upgraded Alphas
and swap it with this machine.  If it boots and loads the new OS, then
this is your problem.

Chris

