david wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> 
> I'm interested in writing a simple network device driver for Digital
> Alpha with digital unix 4.0.
> 
> I couldn't find any documatation about it. The Device driver documation
> for Digital Unix doesn't deal with network device drivers.
> 
> Does anyone know where I can get this information ?

Digital will sell the OS source for about $200,000 (don't quote me on
that, but it's what they once quoted me).  Too expensive for me.

For a cheaper (aka free) solution, consult BSD source.  I wrote a
modified slip driver and found the BSD source was nearly 100% DUX
compatible.  

In fact, I found a bug in their terminal handler, looked up the BSD
terminal handler source, and determined where the code had to be
different in order to cause the bug.  In talking to DEC, I had them look
into their DUX terminal handler source, gave them the file name and
approximate position in their code by reading the BSD code (identifier
names matched very well), then said "right at this position you must be
doing something else", and low-and-behold, there was the bug!

Chris

