Martin Scharpf GI/D wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> 
> I have difficulties to set up the client part of DNS on
> a OSF/1 machine. I created a file /etc/resolv.conf with
> entries
> 
> nameserver 193.193.193.193
> nameserver 194.194.194.194
> domain foo.bar.com
> 
> Then I started nslookup which find it's standard nameserver
> and was able to resolve the names I wanted.
> Next I tried ping with this names. ping said 'unknown host'.
> Same with telnet.
> Is there anything special in OSF/1? Maybe NIS (yellow pages)
> conflict?
> 
> TIA     Martin Scharpf
>         BBraun Melsungen AG

You have to edit /edt/svc.conf and change the line with "hosts=" to
include "bind" in whichever order you want host names to be searched.
For example, to use the /etc/hosts file first and then bind, specify
"hosts=local,bind".
-- 
	- Jay Olson (jjo@triton.com)
	Triton Software Group Ltd.



