In article <5pegrp$8s5@aplinfo.jhuapl.edu>, marabldl@aplcore.jhuapl.edu  (David L. Marable) writes:
|>I am trying to figure out how to add SEAGATE 9 GB (ST19171WC) external
|>hard disk to my alpha workstation 200 running OSF1 V3.2.  I read something
|>about using CAM drivers.  Is this the only way?  Are there any more help
|>in adding entries to the cam_data.c?  

You shouldn't need to do anything like that.

	cd /dev
	./MAKEDEV rzN			(N = scsi ID)

then:
	disklabel -wr rzN rzxx

will partition the drive for you (using some default partition sizes which you
will probably want to change).

Graham



