- Writing VMEbus Device Drivers (AA-Q0R7F-TE), June 1997.

Following the examples provided in that documents and the
procedure to obtain either the dynamic or the static installation
and using as interrupt generator a Motorola CPU (68020 + interrupt
generator + timer PCC chip based), we observed the following behaviour:

a) with Digital UNIX it is not possible to use a simple interfacing
   mechanism different from a complete device driver; it is impossible
   to call a claim_vector mechanism or to associate an interrupt vector
   to a signal.
