   8 kB size even if the user requires less. This means that the user,
   after the buffer allocation, does not have to use the unused part of
   the allocated buffer. Example: current buffer size is 1 kB,
   required data transfer 256 bytes, the DMA can transfer up to 8 kB
   and can corrupt the data from 256 to 1 kB.
   Is this true?
   
