As usual, the solution came to me after I posted the message. I'll post
the solution here in case anyone else should need the information.

While I had done MAKEDEV PTY_2, MAKEDEV PTY_3, etc., I had not done
MAKEDEV PTY_1. I assumed that since there were already 32 pty devices
(ptyp0-ptyqf), that I should start with 2. Wrong! Although I had plenty
of pty devices (many more than I need), there was a gap after ptyqf.
MAKEDEV PTY_1 gave me a bunch of ptys starting with ptyr0.
Richard Nelson wrote:

> Were getting the error message "telnetd: All network ports in use"
> when
