Sumit Jain wrote:
> 
> Hello,
> 
> I have two UNIX machines, one running OSF1 V3.2 and the other running
> OSF1 V4.0
> 
> Both have the same lex executiable located in /usr/ccs/bin
> 
> I run lex on file.l (lex file.l) and the file goes through cleanly on
> OSF1 V3.2.
> 
> When I run the same file on OSF1 V4.0 I get the following warning:
> lex: (Warning) bad state 104 175
> 
> Is there a new version of lex avaliable for OSF1 V4.0??
> Is there a flag that I can use that would eleminate this warning.
LEX was upgraded to Unix95 compliance for DU V4.0. The main
compatibility issue is the /usr/ccs/lib/ncform and /usr/ccs/lib/ncpform.
The main compatibility with the state tables is that the exclusive start
state feature was added in V4.0. You should be able to use the V4.0 LEX
on V3.2 or vice versa, but you need to have the same skeleton files.

