I'm not sure about DU3.2G, but on 4.0, regardless of the number of pty's
you have MAKEDEV'ed 
and any other kernel settings, you must have a suitable entry in
/etc/sysconfigtab like:

pts:
                  <tab>nptys = 512

where <tab> is a tab character. This example sets the number of telnetd
daemons to 512.

If this is not the case then check to make sure that the /dev/ttyr?
series of pseudo-tty's actually exists. I've had this problem once where
the p,q and s series existed, but for some reason MAKEDEV PTY_1 didn't work
properly and there were no r's IYSWIM.

Hope this is some help.

Steven Berry.

