barney dalton wrote:
> 
> How do I change the screen resolution? Is its a kernel option or is at
> the device level? What command does the trick?
> 
> thanks
> barney

Here is the answer:

Digital Unix Vers. 4.x

You must change the entry in these file(s)

1.) /usr/dt/config/Xservers (use the CDE)

:0   Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X :0 -nice -2 -screen0 1280
                                                             ^^^^
this is the resolution 1280x1024

and/or

2.) /var/X11/xdm/Xservers  (use the xdm)

   :0 local /usr/bin/X11/X  -nice -2 -screen0 1280
                                              ^^^^
Joerg-Uwe
