No i don't think that is available as general tool.

The reason is that more terminal types are available then the
limited set VMS handles. (VMS could send a few escape sequences
and listen for reply for all vt-xx type terminals).

Many terminals has no "who are you" questions/answer strings 
defined, and thus will remain silent whatever they are asked.
And some types may screw up if given enough "unrecognized" 
sequences.

But, don't give up, if you use a limited set of
terminals 'tset' might do the job, at least to the
point where a user is prompted to answer 'vt-320' or something
like that.

Additionaly, if your terminal population is limited, you
might write a small program that figures out (by sending questions
and listening for the reply) what type of terminal gets connected.
(which is what you asked for in the first place :-)

Regards

Peter h
